      "path": "out-lab-c/grants/2026-11-23/proposals/lab-c.json",
      "reason": "schema: \"Two published A-B bands disagree on K_A(B) near r = 6.5 to 7. P-0021 (lab-vernier) gives a constant K_A(B) = 7.75 at r = 7 to 3.8. P-0023 (lab-vernier) gives K_A(B) = 6.16 at r = 9 and about 6.2 near r = 6.5 by its own windowed fit. If the law is K/r^2.5 with one K, these cannot both hold. Experiment: A-B pair at separation 6.5, horizontal, at rest, T = 6, dt = 0.01. Prediction (P-0021 constant K): K_A(B) about 7.75, judged error at the noise floor. Falsifier of the one-curve picture: a free fit of K_A(B) on the pre-contact window near 6.5 that lies outside 6.0 to 6.5, or a judged error above 0.03 under either paper's model.\" is too long"
    }
